# What is the newest Go release upstream?
#
# This repo ships ONE line (see UPSTREAM_VERSION) and is capped to it, so it can never tell you
# that a new line exists -- that is exactly what the cap prevents. This file is the uncapped
# tracker: Renovate bumps LATEST_GO whenever upstream Go moves, and the PR is the notification.
#
# When the bump crosses a MINOR (1.26.x -> 1.27.0), that is the signal to decide whether to create
# ModernMavericks/golang-127. See the commits that retired lines/ and made this repo ship one line
# from the root (fae9e3f "refactor: retire lines/, ship one line from the repo root" and ec77028
# "ci: build one line, not a matrix -- unblock the stuck Renovate PRs"); docs/ is gitignored here
# and not present in a clone.
# Merging the PR records that you have seen it; it changes nothing about what this repo builds.
LATEST_GO=1.27.1
